<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Sign in with Apple.

		Required by App Store Review Guideline 4.8 whenever an app offers a
		third-party login, and this one offers Google — so shipping iOS without
		this entitlement is an automatic rejection.

		The matching capability must also be enabled on the App ID in the Apple
		Developer portal, otherwise the entitlement is stripped at signing time
		and the authorization request fails at runtime with error 1000.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		Universal Links.

		The iOS counterpart to Android's App Links. Requires
		https://midoctor.in/.well-known/apple-app-site-association to be served
		over HTTPS with no redirect, and the Associated Domains capability
		enabled on the App ID — without both, iOS silently ignores this and the
		links open in Safari.

		`applinks:` only. `webcredentials:` is deliberately absent: this app has
		no password to share with a website.
	-->
	<!--
		Push notifications.

		`development` here, and that is deliberate rather than an oversight:
		Xcode rewrites this to `production` when it exports a release build, so
		a hard-coded `production` breaks every debug install instead. What it
		cannot do is invent the entitlement, which is why it is declared.

		Also required, and none of it lives in this repo:
		  - Push Notifications capability enabled on the App ID.
		  - An APNs auth key (.p8) uploaded to the Firebase project. Without it
		    FCM accepts the send and silently delivers nothing to iOS.
		  - Background Modes → Remote notifications, if a notification should be
		    able to wake the app rather than only appear.

		Until the APNs key is uploaded, iOS push fails soundlessly: no error on
		the client, a success from FCM, and nothing on the device.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:midoctor.in</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
